    "summary": "Tesla is undergoing a profound strategic transition from a high-volume electric vehicle manufacturer to a physical artificial intelligence and autonomous robotics ecosystem. While core automotive deliveries and overall revenue have demonstrated resilient top-line expansion alongside accelerated growth in utility-scale energy storage deployments, the company is enduring substantial near-term profitability pressure. Operating margins have compressed due to reduced regulatory credit revenues, pricing adjustments, and an aggressive escalation in capital expenditures dedicated to AI training compute, custom silicon, and next-generation production lines. The long-term investment narrative increasingly hinges on successful commercialization of autonomous ride-hailing networks, full self-driving software adoption, and humanoid robotics scaling.",
